//@version=6
// ==============================================================================================
//                     S M C   S U P P L Y   &   D E M A N D   Z O N E S
// ==============================================================================================
//
//  Indicator Name : SMC Supply & Demand Zones
//  Author         : Michael_Fx_Trader
//  Version        : v6.0 - July 2026
//  Pine Version   : Pine Script v6
//  Script Type    : Overlay indicator (plots on the price chart)
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  A U T H O R   V E R I F I C A T I O N   D E C L A R A T I O N
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  I am Michael_Fx_Trader, the publisher and sole original author of this exact
//  implementation of "SMC Supply & Demand Zones." I designed the architecture of this tool, wrote
//  every line of the Pine Script v6 code contained in this file, tested it across multiple asset
//  classes and timeframes, and I take full and sole ownership and responsibility for it.
//
//  Specifically, I independently designed and coded: the displacement-based zone origin detection
//  that finds the bases from which price left with conviction; the ATR-relative displacement test
//  that keeps that detection valid on every instrument and price magnitude; the zone construction
//  with its gradient body and its solid proximal boundary; the per-zone live tracking engine that
//  counts every retest, every breakout and every hold and prints them on the zone itself; the
//  hold-rate calculation that turns those raw counts into a percentage; the test state machine that
//  classifies each interaction as it resolves; the mitigation and break logic; the fresh-versus-
//  tested visual treatment; the zone clustering that merges overlapping bases; the strength model
//  built from displacement, base tightness and volume; the drawing history manager; and the alert
//  framework.
//
//  This declaration is made for this specific version of the script (v6.0, July 2026). Any future
//  modified version I publish will carry its own updated declaration in this same header.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  O R I G I N A L   I N D I C A T O R   S C R I P T   I M P L E M E N T A T I O N
//  V E R I F I C A T I O N   A N D   D E C L A R A T I O N
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  I verify and declare that this script is an original implementation authored from scratch by
//  Michael_Fx_Trader. No portion of this code was copied, ported, decompiled, translated,
//  reverse-engineered or adapted from any other author's closed-source, invite-only, protected or
//  open-source script. No third-party library and no republished open-source script forms any part
//  of this work, and no other author's zone-detection logic, statistics format or visual system
//  was reproduced.
//
//  I acknowledge openly that the underlying trading concepts are public and widely taught. Supply
//  and demand zones, the idea that price leaving an area with a strong displacement leaves behind
//  unfilled orders, the reading of a return to that area as a retest and a decisive close through
//  it as a break, and the distinction between a fresh untested zone and one that has already been
//  tested, are all common knowledge across the trading community and belong to no single author.
//
//  My original contribution, and what this declaration covers, is the specific code
//  implementation: my own displacement-based origin detection, my own ATR-relative thresholds, my
//  own per-zone retest, breakout and hold counting engine, my own hold-rate statistics, my own
//  test state machine, my own clustering, my own strength model, and my own presentation layer.
//  Conceptual overlap with other supply and demand tools is therefore unavoidable and expected,
//  but there is no source-code overlap of any kind with any other author's work.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  W H A T   T H I S   I N D I C A T O R   D O E S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  A supply or demand zone is an area price left in a hurry, leaving unfilled orders behind. When
//  price returns, those orders can push it away again. This tool finds those areas, draws them,
//  and then does the thing most zone tools do not: it keeps a live record of how each individual
//  zone has actually behaved, and prints that record on the zone.
//
//  1) ZONE ORIGIN DETECTION
//     The engine looks for a base, a small cluster of bars, from which price then departed with a
//     displacement larger than a configurable multiple of ATR. A strong departure is the footprint
//     of unfilled orders. The base of a strong rally becomes a demand zone. The base of a strong
//     drop becomes a supply zone.
//
//  2) ZONES, NOT LINES
//     Each zone is drawn as a band from the base's extreme to its body edge, with a gradient fill
//     and a solid line on the proximal side, the side price will meet first. The zone extends to
//     the right for as long as it remains valid.
//
//  3) PER-ZONE LIVE STATISTICS
//     This is the core of the tool. Every zone carries three running counts, printed on its label
//     and updated live: Retests, how many times price has returned into the zone; Breakouts, how
//     many times price has closed decisively through it; and Held, how many times price entered and
//     was pushed back out without breaking. A hold percentage is calculated from those counts. A
//     zone reading Held 30 of a possible set with a high percentage has repeatedly done its job. A
//     zone that mostly breaks tells you the opposite, and it tells you on the chart.
//
//  4) FRESH VERSUS TESTED
//     A zone that has never been touched is drawn differently from one that has already been
//     tested, because a fresh zone and a heavily worked one are not the same trade.
//
//  5) MITIGATION AND RETIREMENT
//     When price closes decisively beyond a zone, that zone is mitigated. It can be removed or kept
//     dimmed as history, at your choice. The oldest zones are retired automatically so the chart
//     stays readable.
//
//  6) STRENGTH MODEL
//     Beyond the raw counts, each zone carries a strength score built from the size of the
//     departure that formed it, the tightness of its base and the volume behind it, all expressed
//     as dimensionless ratios so the score means the same thing on every instrument.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  U N I V E R S A L   M A R K E T   A N D   T I M E F R A M E   C O M P A T I B I L I T Y
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  No pip value, point distance or instrument-specific constant appears anywhere in the logic.
//  The displacement threshold, the base size, the break buffer, the retest and hold distances and
//  the strength model are all expressed in ATR multiples or as ratios. The same settings therefore
//  behave correctly on Forex, gold and other metals, indices, crypto, futures and equities, from
//  seconds charts to monthly, with no adjustment.
//
//  The volume term in the strength model uses a Universal Activity source: real chart volume where
//  the feed publishes it, otherwise a synthetic participation estimate derived from range and
//  candle efficiency, so the strength model never breaks on volume-less spot Forex or metals feeds.
//  Zone detection and all statistics work with or without volume.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  L I V E   B E H A V I O U R   A N D   R E P A I N T I N G   S T A T E M E N T
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  A zone is created only after its displacement has been confirmed on closed bars, so a zone
//  never appears on an unfinished candle and never vanishes afterwards. A zone's origin, its base
//  extreme and its proximal line are fixed at creation and never move.
//
//  The statistics update live, which is the entire point: as price interacts with a zone, its
//  retest, breakout and hold counts advance and its hold percentage recalculates. These are an
//  observed record of what has already happened on the loaded history, not a prediction, and they
//  are accumulated on closed bars so a completed interaction is never uncounted or double counted.
//
//  No request.security call is used by the detection or statistics engine, so there is no
//  higher-timeframe lookahead of any kind.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  D I S C L A I M E R
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  This tool is for educational and informational purposes only. It does not constitute financial
//  advice. Trading involves risk; past patterns do not guarantee future results. The hold-rate
//  statistics describe what has already happened on the loaded history and are not a prediction of
//  future outcomes. Use proper risk management and consult a licensed financial advisor before
//  trading real capital.
// ==============================================================================================

indicator("SMC Supply & Demand Zones", "S&D Zones", overlay = true, max_boxes_count = 500, max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500, max_bars_back = 1000)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  I N P U T S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
gDet = "=====  ZONE DETECTION  ====="
baseBars   = input.int(3,    "Max Base Bars",           minval = 1, maxval = 10, group = gDet, tooltip = "How many bars the consolidation base before a displacement may span.")
dispMult   = input.float(1.8,"Displacement (x ATR)",    minval = 0.3, maxval = 10, step = 0.1, group = gDet, tooltip = "How large the move away from the base must be, in ATR multiples, to leave a zone behind. Higher means fewer, stronger zones.")
atrLen     = input.int(14,   "ATR Length",              minval = 2, maxval = 200, group = gDet)
zoneEdge   = input.string("Body", "Zone Far Edge", options = ["Body", "Wick"], group = gDet, tooltip = "Body draws the zone to the base candles' body edge. Wick draws it to their extreme.")
maxZones   = input.int(12,   "Max Zones Per Side",      minval = 1, maxval = 40, group = gDet)
mergeATR   = input.float(0.6,"Merge Overlapping (x ATR)", minval = 0.0, maxval = 3, step = 0.1, group = gDet, tooltip = "New zones forming within this distance of an existing one on the same side are merged in.")

gStat = "=====  ZONE STATISTICS  ====="
statsOn    = input.bool(true, "Track Retest / Breakout / Held", group = gStat, tooltip = "Counts every interaction with each zone and prints the running totals and hold rate on the zone. Observed record, not a projection.")
retestATR  = input.float(0.15,"Retest Depth (x ATR)", minval = 0.0, maxval = 2, step = 0.05, group = gStat, tooltip = "How far into the zone price must reach to register as a retest.")
holdATR    = input.float(0.8, "Hold Confirmed At (x ATR)", minval = 0.1, maxval = 5, step = 0.1, group = gStat, tooltip = "How far price must travel back away from the zone before a retest counts as held.")
breakBuf   = input.float(0.25,"Break Buffer (x ATR)", minval = 0.0, maxval = 3, step = 0.05, group = gStat, tooltip = "How far beyond the zone price must close for it to count as a breakout.")

gMit = "=====  MITIGATION  ====="
removeBrk  = input.bool(false, "Remove Mitigated Zones", group = gMit, tooltip = "OFF keeps a broken zone drawn but dimmed as history. ON removes it.")
mitClose   = input.bool(true, "Mitigate On Close Only", group = gMit, tooltip = "ON requires a close beyond the zone. OFF allows a wick beyond it to mitigate.")

gVis = "=====  VISUALS  ====="
showZones  = input.bool(true, "Show Zones", group = gVis)
extendR    = input.int(30, "Extend Right (bars)", minval = 0, maxval = 300, group = gVis)
freshMark  = input.bool(true, "Distinguish Fresh Zones", group = gVis)
showLabel  = input.bool(true, "Show Statistics Label", group = gVis)
showStr    = input.bool(true, "Show Strength In Label", group = gVis)
lblSize    = input.string("Small", "Label Size", options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal"], group = gVis)
showTable  = input.bool(true, "Show Summary Table", group = gVis)
tablePos   = input.string("Top Right", "Table Position", options = ["Top Left", "Left Center", "Bottom Left", "Top Right", "Bottom Right"], group = gVis)

gAct = "=====  ACTIVITY SOURCE  (strength model)  ====="
actMode = input.string("Auto", "Volume Source", options = ["Auto", "Chart Volume Only", "Synthetic Estimate"], group = gAct)

gSty = "=====  STYLE  ====="
colSup   = input.color(#ef5350, "Supply Zone", group = gSty, inline = "a")
colDem   = input.color(#26c6a8, "Demand Zone", group = gSty, inline = "a")
zoneTrans= input.int(78, "Zone Transparency", minval = 0, maxval = 100, group = gSty)
mitTrans = input.int(92, "Mitigated Transparency", minval = 0, maxval = 100, group = gSty)
colTxtS  = input.color(#ef5350, "Supply Text", group = gSty, inline = "b")
colTxtD  = input.color(#1e9e86, "Demand Text", group = gSty, inline = "b")
colTblBg = input.color(#0b1020, "Table Background", group = gSty)
colTblTx = input.color(#d1d4dc, "Table Text", group = gSty)

string szL = lblSize == "Tiny" ? size.tiny : lblSize == "Normal" ? size.normal : size.small

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  U N I V E R S A L   A C T I V I T Y   ( for the strength model only )
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
float rawVol  = nz(volume)
bool  hasReal = ta.cum(rawVol) > 0 and not na(volume)
float trueR   = ta.tr(true)
float baseATR = ta.atr(20)
float bodyEff = trueR > 0 ? math.abs(close - open) / trueR : 0.0
float synth   = baseATR > 0 ? math.max(0.0, (trueR / baseATR) * (0.55 + 0.45 * bodyEff) * 1000.0) : 0.0
float actVol  = actMode == "Chart Volume Only" ? rawVol : actMode == "Synthetic Estimate" ? synth : (hasReal ? rawVol : synth)
float actAvg  = ta.sma(actVol, 20)

float atr = ta.atr(atrLen)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Z O N E   T Y P E   A N D   R E G I S T R Y
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
type Zone
    float top
    float bot
    float prox       // proximal edge, the side price meets first
    bool  isSup
    int   born
    float strength
    int   retests
    int   breaks
    int   holds
    int   state      // 0 idle, 1 inside a test
    bool  fresh
    bool  dead
    box   bx
    line  ln
    label lb

var array<Zone> zones = array.new<Zone>()

bool newSup   = false
bool newDem   = false
bool anyBreak = false
bool anyHold  = false
bool anyRetest= false

method wipe(Zone z) =>
    box.delete(z.bx)
    line.delete(z.ln)
    label.delete(z.lb)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Z O N E   O R I G I N   D E T E C T I O N
//  A base of up to baseBars, then a displacement larger than dispMult x ATR leaving it. The base
//  of a strong up-move is demand; the base of a strong down-move is supply.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
strengthOf(int originBar, int baseLen, float dispSize, float baseHi, float baseLo) =>
    float a = nz(atr[originBar])
    float compDisp = a > 0 ? math.min(dispSize / a / math.max(dispMult, 0.1), 2.0) / 2.0 : 0.0
    float tight = a > 0 ? math.max(0.0, 1.0 - (baseHi - baseLo) / (a * 2.0)) : 0.0
    float av = nz(actAvg[originBar])
    float vr = av > 0 ? math.min(nz(actVol[originBar]) / av / 2.0, 1.0) : 0.5
    math.max(0.0, math.min(10.0, (compDisp * 0.5 + tight * 0.25 + vr * 0.25) * 10.0))

if barstate.isconfirmed and not na(atr) and atr > 0 and bar_index > baseBars + atrLen + 2
    float mergeD = atr * mergeATR
    // the displacement candle is the one that just closed at [1]; the base is the bars before it
    float dispOpen = open[1]
    float dispClose = close[1]
    float disp = dispClose - dispOpen
    bool  up   = disp > 0

    if math.abs(disp) > atr * dispMult
        // measure the base immediately behind the displacement
        float bHi = na
        float bLo = na
        for k = 2 to baseBars + 1
            bHi := na(bHi) ? high[k] : math.max(bHi, high[k])
            bLo := na(bLo) ? low[k]  : math.min(bLo, low[k])

        if not na(bHi) and not na(bLo)
            bool isSup = not up
            // body-edge extremes across the base bars
            float bodyHi = na
            float bodyLo = na
            for k = 2 to baseBars + 1
                bodyHi := na(bodyHi) ? math.max(open[k], close[k]) : math.max(bodyHi, math.max(open[k], close[k]))
                bodyLo := na(bodyLo) ? math.min(open[k], close[k]) : math.min(bodyLo, math.min(open[k], close[k]))
            float top = zoneEdge == "Wick" ? bHi : nz(bodyHi, bHi)
            float bot = zoneEdge == "Wick" ? bLo : nz(bodyLo, bLo)
            if top <= bot
                top := bHi
                bot := bLo

            float prox = isSup ? bot : top
            int   originBar = bar_index - (baseBars + 1)
            float strv = strengthOf(baseBars + 1, baseBars, math.abs(disp), bHi, bLo)

            // merge into an existing overlapping same-side zone
            int hit = -1
            if zones.size() > 0
                for m = 0 to zones.size() - 1
                    Zone z = zones.get(m)
                    if z.isSup == isSup and not z.dead and math.abs(((z.top + z.bot) / 2) - ((top + bot) / 2)) <= mergeD
                        hit := m
            if hit >= 0
                Zone z = zones.get(hit)
                z.top := math.max(z.top, top)
                z.bot := math.min(z.bot, bot)
                z.prox := z.isSup ? z.bot : z.top
                z.strength := math.max(z.strength, strv)
            else
                Zone z = Zone.new()
                z.top := top
                z.bot := bot
                z.prox := prox
                z.isSup := isSup
                z.born := math.max(0, bar_index - (baseBars + 2))
                z.strength := strv
                z.retests := 0
                z.breaks := 0
                z.holds := 0
                z.state := 0
                z.fresh := true
                z.dead := false
                zones.push(z)
                if isSup
                    newSup := true
                else
                    newDem := true

            // enforce per-side cap
            int nS = 0
            int nD = 0
            for m = zones.size() - 1 to 0
                Zone z = zones.get(m)
                if z.isSup
                    nS += 1
                    if nS > maxZones
                        z.wipe()
                        zones.remove(m)
                else
                    nD += 1
                    if nD > maxZones
                        z.wipe()
                        zones.remove(m)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  P E R - Z O N E   T E S T   T R A C K I N G   ( retest / breakout / held )
//  Each interaction is classified as it resolves. A retest that leaves without breaking is a hold.
//  A close beyond the zone is a breakout. Counts accumulate on closed bars.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
if statsOn and barstate.isconfirmed and not na(atr) and atr > 0 and zones.size() > 0
    float rd = atr * retestATR
    float hd = atr * holdATR
    float bd = atr * breakBuf
    for m = zones.size() - 1 to 0
        Zone z = zones.get(m)
        if not z.dead
            float zHi = z.top
            float zLo = z.bot

            // entry into the zone starts a test
            bool entered = high >= zLo - rd and low <= zHi + rd
            if z.state == 0 and entered
                z.state := 1
                z.retests += 1
                z.fresh := false
                anyRetest := true

            // breakout: a decisive close through the far side
            bool broke = z.isSup ? (mitClose ? close > zHi + bd : high > zHi + bd) : (mitClose ? close < zLo - bd : low < zLo - bd)
            if broke
                z.breaks += 1
                z.dead := true
                anyBreak := true
                z.state := 0
                if removeBrk
                    z.wipe()
                    zones.remove(m)
            else if z.state == 1
                // held: price travelled back away from the proximal edge without breaking
                float away = z.isSup ? z.prox - high : low - z.prox
                if away >= hd
                    z.holds += 1
                    anyHold := true
                    z.state := 0

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  D R A W I N G
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
holdPct(Zone z) =>
    int denom = z.holds + z.breaks
    denom > 0 ? z.holds * 100.0 / denom : na

if barstate.islast and showZones and zones.size() > 0
    for m = 0 to zones.size() - 1
        Zone z = zones.get(m)
        color base = z.isSup ? colSup : colDem
        color txtC = z.isSup ? colTxtS : colTxtD
        int   trans = z.dead ? mitTrans : zoneTrans
        int   right = bar_index + extendR

        z.wipe()

        // zone body with a solid proximal line
        z.bx := box.new(z.born, z.top, right, z.bot, xloc = xloc.bar_index, border_color = color.new(base, 100), bgcolor = color.new(base, trans))
        z.ln := line.new(z.born, z.prox, right, z.prox, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(base, z.dead ? 55 : 10), width = 2)

        // fresh untested zones get a dashed proximal line to set them apart
        if freshMark and z.fresh and not z.dead
            line.set_style(z.ln, line.style_dashed)

        if showLabel
            string txt = ""
            if statsOn
                float hp = holdPct(z)
                txt := "Retests: " + str.tostring(z.retests) + "  -  Breakouts: " + str.tostring(z.breaks) + "  -  Held: " + str.tostring(z.holds) + (na(hp) ? "" : "  (" + str.tostring(hp, "#") + "%)")
            else
                txt := z.isSup ? "Supply" : "Demand"
            if showStr
                txt := txt + "   S" + str.tostring(z.strength, "#.#")
            if z.dead
                txt := txt + "   mitigated"
            z.lb := label.new(right, z.prox, txt, xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = z.isSup ? label.style_label_lower_left : label.style_label_upper_left, color = color.new(base, 100), textcolor = txtC, size = szL)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  S U M M A R Y   T A B L E
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
var table tbl = na

tablePosition() =>
    tablePos == "Top Left" ? position.top_left : tablePos == "Bottom Left" ? position.bottom_left : tablePos == "Top Right" ? position.top_right : tablePos == "Bottom Right" ? position.bottom_right : position.middle_left

if barstate.islast and showTable
    table.delete(tbl)

    int nSup = 0
    int nDem = 0
    int nFresh = 0
    int totHold = 0
    int totBreak = 0
    float nearDist = na
    string nearTxt = "-"
    color  nearCol = colTblTx

    if zones.size() > 0
        for m = 0 to zones.size() - 1
            Zone z = zones.get(m)
            if not z.dead
                if z.isSup
                    nSup += 1
                else
                    nDem += 1
                if z.fresh
                    nFresh += 1
                totHold += z.holds
                totBreak += z.breaks
                float d = math.abs(close - z.prox)
                if na(nearDist) or d < nearDist
                    nearDist := d
                    nearTxt := (z.isSup ? "Supply " : "Demand ") + str.tostring(z.prox, format.mintick)
                    nearCol := z.isSup ? colTxtS : colTxtD

    int denom = totHold + totBreak
    float aggHold = denom > 0 ? totHold * 100.0 / denom : na

    tbl := table.new(tablePosition(), 2, 5, border_width = 1, border_color = color.new(colTblTx, 82), frame_width = 1, frame_color = color.new(colTblTx, 72))
    color bgH = color.new(colTblBg, 0)
    color bgR = color.new(colTblBg, 12)

    table.cell(tbl, 0, 0, "SMC SUPPLY & DEMAND", bgcolor = bgH, text_color = #f0b90b, text_size = size.small)
    table.merge_cells(tbl, 0, 0, 1, 0)

    table.cell(tbl, 0, 1, "Active Zones", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 1, str.tostring(nSup) + " supply   " + str.tostring(nDem) + " demand", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(tbl, 0, 2, "Fresh (untested)", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 2, str.tostring(nFresh), bgcolor = bgR, text_color = nFresh > 0 ? colDem : colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(tbl, 0, 3, "Nearest Zone", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 3, nearTxt, bgcolor = bgR, text_color = nearCol, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(tbl, 0, 4, "Overall Hold Rate", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 4, na(aggHold) ? "-" : str.tostring(aggHold, "#") + "%   (" + str.tostring(denom) + " resolved)", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = na(aggHold) ? colTblTx : denom < 10 ? color.new(colTblTx, 40) : aggHold >= 50 ? colDem : colSup, text_size = size.tiny)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  A L E R T S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
alertcondition(newSup,    "S&D - New Supply Zone",  "SMC Supply & Demand Zones: a new supply zone formed on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(newDem,    "S&D - New Demand Zone",  "SMC Supply & Demand Zones: a new demand zone formed on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(anyRetest, "S&D - Zone Retested",    "SMC Supply & Demand Zones: price is retesting a zone on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(anyHold,   "S&D - Zone Held",        "SMC Supply & Demand Zones: a zone held and pushed price away on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(anyBreak,  "S&D - Zone Broken",      "SMC Supply & Demand Zones: a zone was broken on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")

if newSup
    alert("S&D New Supply - " + syminfo.ticker + " " + timeframe.period, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if newDem
    alert("S&D New Demand - " + syminfo.ticker + " " + timeframe.period, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if anyBreak
    alert("S&D Zone Broken - " + syminfo.ticker + " " + timeframe.period, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  D A T A   W I N D O W   O U T P U T S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
plot(zones.size(), "Zones Tracked", color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)
plot(atr,          "ATR",           color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)
